cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use GeoSync in academic research, industry reports, or derivative
  work, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "GeoSync: Verification-First Quantitative Market-Structure Research Platform"
abstract: >-
  GeoSync is a verification-first quantitative research platform for
  falsifiable market-structure hypotheses. It provides physics- and
  neuroscience-inspired instrumentation — Kuramoto phase synchronization,
  Ollivier-Ricci curvature, fractal/DFA dynamics, and free-energy-based
  neuro-symbolic risk control — studied as market-microstructure
  descriptors and exposed through a deterministic event-driven backtester
  and an execution-realism (paper / replay) harness. Every quantitative
  claim is admissible only when bound to an explicit invariant, data
  contract, falsifier, and reproducible artifact, and is promoted no
  further than its declared evidence tier (FACT / MEASURED / SIMULATION /
  HYPOTHESIS; see CLAIMS.md). Project maturity: RESEARCH_ALPHA — live
  market-structure claims rest on synthetic or single-session evidence
  only (governance/project_state.yaml). Limitations: GeoSync is not a
  live-trading system, alpha engine, or investment-advice product, and
  asserts no out-of-sample market edge; it verifies invariants of its own
  computation, not laws of markets (PRODUCT_CATEGORY.md, FORBIDDEN_CLAIMS.md).
